module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.DenseSubsite.InducedTopology
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GeneratedIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Localization
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# A finite-type sheaf of ideals is locally a generated one, and generators agree above a cover

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` and `g_1, …, g_s` be two finite families of
global sections of `𝒪` generating the *same* sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`. The objectwise ideals
`(f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪(U)` and `(g_1, …, g_s) ⊂ 𝒪(U)` they span over an object `U` need not be
equal — membership in `ℐ` is local, which is the warning of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] — but they
become equal above a covering of `U`. That is the step [Stacks, Tag 099E] records only as a
hint: "if `I'` is a finitely generated ideal which also generates `ℐ|_U`, then there exists a
covering `{U_j → U}` such that `I𝒪(U_j) = I'𝒪(U_j)`; this works because both `I` and `I'` are
finitely generated and generate `ℐ|_U`".

The proof is the hint. Each `g_j` is a section of `ℐ` over `U`, hence by the local description
of the ideal sheaf an `𝒪`-linear combination of the `f_i` above some covering sieve of `U`; the
condition "`g_j` is a combination of the `f_i` here" is itself a sieve, because restricting a
combination gives a combination, so that covering sieve is contained in it and it is covering.
Intersecting the `r + s` sieves obtained this way — finitely many, which is exactly where the
finite generation of both families is used — gives one covering sieve above which every
generator of each family lies in the span of the other, so the two spans coincide.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpanSieve`: the sieve of objects over which a given
  global section of `𝒪` is an `𝒪`-linear combination of `f_1, …, f_r`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctorOf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnitOf`: the completion functor
  `E ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, E)` and its unit attached to an arbitrary map `κ : K ⟶ 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)`,
  of which the Čech functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is the case `K = Č(f)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsFinitelyGeneratedOver`: the **finitely-generated locus** of a
  sheaf of ideals — the objects `U` over which `ℐ|_U` is the sheaf of ideals generated by
  finitely many sections of `𝒪(U)`. This is the subcategory `𝒞'` of [Stacks, Tag 099E].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overGlobalSectionRestrict`: the restriction of a global section
  of the structure sheaf of `𝒞/U` along an arrow `W ⟶ U`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpanSieve_mem`: that sieve is covering as soon as the
  section is a section of the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq`: **two finite families of global
  sections generating the same sheaf of ideals span the same ideal of sections above a covering
  sieve of every object.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_augmented`:
  [Stacks, Tag 099F] reduced to an arbitrary augmented object `K ⟶ 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)` whose
  completion functor is idempotent in the three senses of
  `Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_of_completionFunctor`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_generatingSections`: **a sheaf
  of ideals generated by finitely many of its own global sections is the sheaf of ideals those
  sections generate**, the converse of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatingSections`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`: **a
  finite-type sheaf of ideals is, on the slice site over each member of a family of objects
  covering the final object, the sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many sections of the
  structure sheaf there.** This is the passage from the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tags 099E and
  099F] to the regime in which [Stacks, Tag 099B] and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` apply.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsFinitelyGeneratedOver.of_hom`: **the finitely-generated locus
  is stable under arrows**, from
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict`: a
  presentation of `ℐ|_U` by finitely many sections restricts to a presentation of `ℐ|_W` for
  every `W` over `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType`:
  **cover-density of the finitely-generated locus** — for `ℐ` of finite type, *every* object of
  `𝒞` is covered by objects on which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections. This is the
  first step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDenseSubsite_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType`, and
  its `inducedTopology` form
  `isDenseSubsite_inducedTopology_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType`:
  **the inclusion `𝒞' ⟶ 𝒞` is a dense subsite**, which is what the sheaf and sheaf-of-modules
  Comparison Lemmas (`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsDenseSubsite.sheafEquiv`,
  `Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence`) consume.

## Implementation notes

The cover-density statement needs no relativisation of
`exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType` to a slice site:
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` is *by definition* the assertion that
`CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofObjects` is covering at **every** object, not only at a terminal one.
What has to be added is that the locus is stable under arrows, so that the source of every
arrow in that sieve is itself an object of `𝒞'` and the arrow factors through it by the
identity.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sieve_iInf_mem`, that a finite infimum of covering sieves is
covering, is stated for a `Fin`-indexed family and proved by induction from
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.intersection_covering`; the two families of generators are
`Fin`-indexed, so no `Finset` version is needed.

Nothing in this file carries a `@[stacks]` attribute. The generator-independence statement is
one step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E] and not any assertion of that lemma, whose
conclusion is the existence of a global complex `K ⟶ 𝒪`; and the reduction of
[Stacks, Tag 099F] below takes the three properties of the completion functor as hypotheses
rather than proving them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

section Sieves

/-- **A finite infimum of covering sieves is covering.** -/
theorem sieve_iInf_mem {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C) {V : C} :
    ∀ {n : ℕ} (S : Fin n → Sieve V), (∀ i, S i ∈ J V) → (⨅ i, S i) ∈ J V := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero => intro S _; simpa using J.top_mem V
  | succ m ih =>
    intro S hS
    have hsplit : (⨅ i : Fin (m + 1), S i) = S 0 ⊓ ⨅ i : Fin m, S i.succ := by
      refine le_antisymm (le_inf (iInf_le _ 0) (le_iInf fun i ↦ iInf_le _ i.succ)) ?_
      refine le_iInf fun i ↦ ?_
      rcases Fin.eq_zero_or_eq_succ i with rfl | ⟨j, rfl⟩
      · exact inf_le_left
      · exact inf_le_right.trans (iInf_le _ j)
    rw [hsplit]
    exact J.intersection_covering (hS 0) (ih _ fun i ↦ hS i.succ)

end Sieves

section Independence

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r s : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The sieve of objects over which a global section of `𝒪` is an `𝒪`-linear combination of
`f_1, …, f_r`.** It is a sieve because the restriction of a combination is the combination of
the restrictions, the `f_i` being global sections. -/
def sectionSpanSieve (h : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    (V : X.C) : Sieve V where
  arrows := fun {W} _ ↦ globalSectionVal h (op W) ∈ sectionSpan f (op W)
  downward_closed := by
    intro W W' p hp q
    have hq := map_mem_sectionSpan f (Quiver.Hom.op q) hp
    rwa [globalSectionVal_map] at hq

/-- An arrow `p : W ⟶ V` lies in `sectionSpanSieve f h V` exactly when the value of `h` over `W`
lies in the span of the values of `f_1, …, f_r` over `W`. -/
theorem mem_sectionSpanSieve_iff (h : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    {V W : X.C} (p : W ⟶ V) :
    (sectionSpanSieve f h V).arrows p ↔
      globalSectionVal h (op W) ∈ sectionSpan f (op W) := Iff.rfl

/-- **The sieve is covering as soon as the section belongs to the ideal sheaf generated by
`f_1, …, f_r`.** This is the local description of that ideal sheaf,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf`, read as a statement
about the sieve. -/
theorem sectionSpanSieve_mem (h : Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    (V : X.C) (hh : globalSectionVal h (op V) ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj (op V)) :
    sectionSpanSieve f h V ∈ X.J V := by
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hc⟩ := exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f hh
  refine X.J.superset_covering (fun W p hp ↦ ?_) hS
  obtain ⟨c, hcw⟩ := hc p hp
  refine (mem_sectionSpanSieve_iff f h p).2 ((mem_sectionSpan_iff f (op W) _).2 ⟨c, ?_⟩)
  rw [hcw, globalSectionVal_map]

variable (g : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- The sieve above which each member of each of the two families lies in the span of the
other. -/
def spanAgreementSieve (V : X.C) : Sieve V :=
  (⨅ j, sectionSpanSieve f (g j) V) ⊓ ⨅ i, sectionSpanSieve g (f i) V

/-- If each `g_j` is a section over `V` of the ideal sheaf generated by the `f_i`, and each `f_i`
one of the ideal sheaf generated by the `g_j`, then `spanAgreementSieve f g V` is covering. -/
theorem spanAgreementSieve_mem (V : X.C)
    (hgf : ∀ j, globalSectionVal (g j) (op V) ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj (op V))
    (hfg : ∀ i, globalSectionVal (f i) (op V) ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf g).obj (op V)) :
    spanAgreementSieve f g V ∈ X.J V :=
  X.J.intersection_covering
    (sieve_iInf_mem X.J _ fun j ↦ sectionSpanSieve_mem f (g j) V (hgf j))
    (sieve_iInf_mem X.J _ fun i ↦ sectionSpanSieve_mem g (f i) V (hfg i))

/-- The span of the `f_i` over `U` lies in the span of the `g_j` once every `f_i` does. -/
private theorem sectionSpan_le_of_forall_mem (g : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections _) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ)
    (h : ∀ i, globalSectionVal (f i) U ∈ sectionSpan g U) : sectionSpan f U ≤ sectionSpan g U :=
  Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.range_subset_iff.2 h)

/-- Over the source of every arrow of `spanAgreementSieve f g V`, the ideals of sections spanned by
the `f_i` and by the `g_j` are equal. -/
theorem sectionSpan_eq_of_mem_spanAgreementSieve {V W : X.C} (p : W ⟶ V)
    (hp : (spanAgreementSieve f g V).arrows p) :
    sectionSpan f (op W) = sectionSpan g (op W) :=
  le_antisymm (sectionSpan_le_of_forall_mem f g _ fun i ↦ hp.2 _ ⟨i, rfl⟩)
    (sectionSpan_le_of_forall_mem g f _ fun j ↦ hp.1 _ ⟨j, rfl⟩)

/-- **Two finite families of global sections generating the same sheaf of ideals span the same
ideal of sections above a covering sieve of every object.** This is the hint of
[Stacks, Tag 099E]: the objectwise spans `(f_1, …, f_r) ⊂ 𝒪(U)` and `(g_1, …, g_s) ⊂ 𝒪(U)`
differ in general, but they agree after restriction along every arrow of some covering sieve of
`U`, and finitely many generators on each side is exactly what makes the finite intersection of
sieves available. -/
theorem exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq
    (hfg : generatedIdealSheaf f = generatedIdealSheaf g) (V : X.C) :
    ∃ S : Sieve V, S ∈ X.J V ∧
      ∀ ⦃W : X.C⦄ (p : W ⟶ V), S.arrows p → sectionSpan f (op W) = sectionSpan g (op W) :=
  ⟨spanAgreementSieve f g V,
    spanAgreementSieve_mem f g V
      (fun j ↦ hfg ▸ globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf g j (op V))
      (fun i ↦ hfg ▸ globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f i (op V)),
    fun _ p hp ↦ sectionSpan_eq_of_mem_spanAgreementSieve f g p hp⟩

end Independence

section GeneralCompletion

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]

/-- **The completion functor attached to an object `K` of `D(𝒪)`**: the endofunctor
`E ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, E)`. The Čech functor
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is the case
`K = Č(f)`. -/
def completionFunctorOf (K : DerivedCategory
    (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  (derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).obj (op K)

/-- **The completion map attached to an augmented object `κ : K ⟶ 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)`**: the
identification `E = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, E)` followed by the map which `κ` induces on derived
internal Hom into `E`. -/
def completionUnitOf {K : DerivedCategory
    (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (κ : K ⟶ derivedStructureSheaf X) :
    𝟭 (DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⟶
        completionFunctorOf X K :=
  (derivedStructureSheafHomNatIso X).inv ≫ (derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).map κ.op

variable {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- The Čech completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is the completion functor of the extended
alternating Čech complex. -/
theorem completionFunctorOf_extendedAlternatingCech :
    completionFunctorOf X (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (extendedAlternatingCech X f)) =
      completionFunctor X f := rfl

/-- The Čech completion map of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is the completion map of the Čech
augmentation. -/
theorem completionUnitOf_cechAugmentation :
    completionUnitOf X (DerivedCategory.Q.map (cechAugmentation X f)) = completionUnit X f := rfl

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099F] for an arbitrary augmented object of `D(𝒪)`.** If `κ : K ⟶ 𝒪` is a map
of `D(𝒪)` such that every `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K, E)` is derived complete along `ℐ`, that the
completion map is invertible on derived-complete objects, and that the completion functor
carries every completion map to an isomorphism, then the inclusion of the derived-complete
objects into `D(𝒪)` has a left adjoint.

The three hypotheses are those of
`Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_of_completionFunctor`, and the third is not implied by
the first two — see the counterexample
`Stacks.Algebraization.CompletionUnitSharpness.exists_completionFunctor_and_not_isRightAdjoint_ι`.
At `K = Č(f)` and `ℐ` generated by `f_1, …, f_r` all three are discharged, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`. -/
theorem isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_augmented
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
    {K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (κ : K ⟶ derivedStructureSheaf X)
    (hΦ : ∀ E, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I ((completionFunctorOf X K).obj E))
    (hη : ∀ E, IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I E → IsIso ((completionUnitOf X κ).app E))
    (hΦη : ∀ E, IsIso ((completionFunctorOf X K).map ((completionUnitOf X κ).app E))) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I)).IsRightAdjoint :=
  Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_of_completionFunctor (completionUnitOf X κ) hΦ hη hΦη

end GeneralCompletion

section FiniteGenerators

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- The value over `U` of a section of an ideal subsheaf of `𝒪`, as a section of `𝒪`. -/
def idealSectionVal (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}).obj U := (s.val U).1

/-- The value over `U` of a section of `𝓘` lies in `𝓘(U)`. -/
theorem idealSectionVal_mem (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U ∈ 𝓘.obj U := (s.val U).2

/-- The values of a section of `𝓘` are compatible with the restriction maps of `𝒪`. -/
theorem idealSectionVal_map (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V) :
    (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}).map g (idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U) =
      idealSectionVal 𝓘 s V :=
  congrArg Subtype.val (s.property g)

/-- **A section of an ideal subsheaf of `𝒪`, read as a global section of the structure
presheaf.** A section of `ℐ` over the whole site is a compatible family of local sections of
`ℐ`, hence of `𝒪`. -/
def globalSectionOfIdealSection (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) :
    Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm
    ⟨idealSectionVal 𝓘 s, fun g ↦ idealSectionVal_map 𝓘 s g⟩

/-- The value over `U` of `globalSectionOfIdealSection 𝓘 s` is the value of `s` over `U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfIdealSection (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections)
    (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (globalSectionOfIdealSection 𝓘 s) U = idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U := by
  show (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _
    ((Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm _)).val U = _
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

variable [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A family of sections of `ℐ` all of whose values lie in a second ideal subsheaf `𝓚`, read as
sections of `𝓚`. -/
def idealSectionTransfer {𝓚 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) (h : ∀ U, idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U ∈ 𝓚.obj U) :
    𝓚.toSheafOfModules.sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun U ↦ ⟨idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U, h U⟩)
    fun _ _ f ↦ Subtype.ext (idealSectionVal_map 𝓘 s f)

/-- The image of `idealSectionTransfer 𝓘 s h` under the inclusion `𝓚 ⟶ 𝒪` is the image of `s`
under the inclusion `𝓘 ⟶ 𝒪`. -/
theorem sectionsMap_ι_idealSectionTransfer
    {𝓚 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (s : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.sections) (h : ∀ U, idealSectionVal 𝓘 s U ∈ 𝓚.obj U) :
    PresheafOfModules.sectionsMap 𝓚.ι.val (idealSectionTransfer 𝓘 s h) =
      PresheafOfModules.sectionsMap 𝓘.ι.val s :=
  PresheafOfModules.sections_ext _ _ fun _ ↦ by
    first
      | rfl
      | simp [PresheafOfModules.sectionsMap, idealSectionTransfer, idealSectionVal]

/-- **An ideal subsheaf of `𝒪` generated by finitely many of its own global sections is the
sheaf of ideals those sections generate.** This is the passage missing between
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, whose local data is a family of generating sections, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf`, which is what the Čech complex of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] is built from: the inclusion `𝒪^I ⟶ ℐ` named by the generators is an
epimorphism, so every section of `ℐ` is locally a combination of them, and membership in any
sheaf of ideals containing them is local.

The converse, that a `generatedIdealSheaf` has such a family, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatingSections`. -/
theorem exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_generatingSections
    (σ : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.GeneratingSections) [Finite σ.I] :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})),
      𝓘 = generatedIdealSheaf f := by
  obtain ⟨r, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin σ.I
  refine ⟨r, fun i ↦ globalSectionOfIdealSection 𝓘 (σ.s (e.symm i)), ?_⟩
  refine eq_generatedIdealSheaf _ (fun i U ↦ ?_) (fun 𝓚 h ↦ ?_)
  · rw [globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfIdealSection]
    exact idealSectionVal_mem 𝓘 _ U
  · have h' : ∀ (i : σ.I) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), idealSectionVal 𝓘 (σ.s i) U ∈ 𝓚.obj U := by
      intro i U
      have := h (e i) U
      rwa [globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfIdealSection, Equiv.symm_apply_apply] at this
    set ψ : SheafOfModules.free (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) σ.I ⟶
        𝓚.toSheafOfModules :=
      𝓚.toSheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv.symm
        (fun i ↦ idealSectionTransfer 𝓘 (σ.s i) (h' i)) with hψ
    have hfac : ψ ≫ 𝓚.ι = σ.π ≫ 𝓘.ι := by
      rw [hψ, SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv_symm_comp,
        show σ.π = 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv.symm σ.s from rfl,
        SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv_symm_comp]
      refine congrArg (SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv _).symm (funext fun i ↦ ?_)
      exact sectionsMap_ι_idealSectionTransfer 𝓘 (σ.s i) (h' i)
    refine SheafOfModules.Submodule.le_iff.2 (fun V x hx ↦ ?_)
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hsec⟩ :=
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.exists_covering_of_epi σ.π
        (V := V.unop) (⟨x, hx⟩ : ToType (𝓘.toSheafOfModules.val.obj V))
    refine 𝓚.isSheaf x (X.J.superset_covering (fun W g hg ↦ ?_) hS)
    show ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val).map g.op x ∈
        𝓚.obj (op W)
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hsec g hg
    have hcomp : ((ψ ≫ 𝓚.ι).val.app (op W)) t = ((σ.π ≫ 𝓘.ι).val.app (op W)) t :=
      congrArg (fun φ : SheafOfModules.free (R := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          σ.I ⟶ SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ↦
            (φ.val.app (op W)) t) hfac
    have hleft : ((ψ ≫ 𝓚.ι).val.app (op W)) t = (ψ.val.app (op W) t).1 := rfl
    have hright : ((σ.π ≫ 𝓘.ι).val.app (op W)) t = (σ.π.val.app (op W) t).1 := rfl
    rw [hleft, hright] at hcomp
    have h0 : ((σ.π.val.app (op W)) t).1 =
        ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val).map g.op x :=
              congrArg Subtype.val ht
    rw [← h0, ← hcomp]
    exact (ψ.val.app (op W) t).2

end FiniteGenerators

section FiniteTypeCover

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- The sheaf of modules of a sheaf of ideals restricted to a slice site is the restriction of
its sheaf of modules, by definition. -/
theorem toSheafOfModules_overIdeal (U : X.C) :
    (overIdeal 𝓘 U).toSheafOfModules = 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.over U := rfl

/-- **A sheaf of ideals whose restriction to a slice site is generated by finitely many sections
there is, on that slice site, the sheaf of ideals those sections generate.** -/
theorem exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal (U : X.C)
    [HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [(X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (σ : (𝓘.toSheafOfModules.over U).GeneratingSections) [Finite σ.I] :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})),
      overIdeal 𝓘 U = generatedIdealSheaf f := by
  have h1 : HasSheafify (X.over U).J AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
    inferInstanceAs (HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w})
  have h2 : (X.over U).J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
    inferInstanceAs ((X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w})
  exact exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_generatingSections (X := X.over U) (overIdeal 𝓘 U) σ

/-- **A finite-type sheaf of ideals is, above a covering of the final object, generated by
finitely many sections.** This is the passage from `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` — the source's
own hypothesis in [Stacks, Tags 099E and 099F] — to
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf`, the sheaf of ideals that the Čech complex of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] and the completion functor of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` are built
from: there is a family of objects covering the final object such that the restriction of `ℐ` to
each member's slice site is the sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many sections of the
structure sheaf there. -/
theorem exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType) :
    ∃ (ι : Type u) (V : ι → X.C) (_ : X.J.CoversTop V) (r : ι → ℕ)
      (f : ∀ i, Fin (r i) →
        Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over (V i)).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})),
      ∀ i, overIdeal 𝓘 (V i) = generatedIdealSheaf (f i) := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := h.exists_localGeneratorsData
  have hfin : ∀ i : σ.I, Finite (σ.generators i).I := fun i ↦ (hσ.isFiniteType i).finite
  have hex : ∀ i : σ.I, ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r →
      Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over (σ.X i)).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})),
      overIdeal 𝓘 (σ.X i) = generatedIdealSheaf f := fun i ↦
    have := hfin i
    exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal 𝓘 (σ.X i) (σ.generators i)
  choose r f hf using hex
  exact ⟨σ.I, σ.X, σ.coversTop, r, f, hf⟩

end FiniteTypeCover

section CoverDense

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}}

/-- **The restriction along an arrow `h : W ⟶ U` of the base of a global section of the
structure sheaf of the slice site over `U`.** Its value over an object `V ⟶ W` of `𝒞/W` is the
value of the given section over the object `V ⟶ W ⟶ U` of `𝒞/U`, i.e. over
`(CategoryTheory.Over.map h).obj V`; the family is compatible because the given one is. -/
def overGlobalSectionRestrict {U W : X.C} (h : W ⟶ U)
    (g : Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})) :
    Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over W).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}) :=
  (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).symm
    ⟨fun V ↦ globalSectionVal g (op ((Over.map h).obj V.unop)),
      fun {_ _} φ ↦ globalSectionVal_map g ((Over.map h).map φ.unop).op⟩

/-- The value of `overGlobalSectionRestrict h g` over an object `V` of `𝒞/W` is the value of `g`
over `(CategoryTheory.Over.map h).obj V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem globalSectionVal_overGlobalSectionRestrict {U W : X.C} (h : W ⟶ U)
    (g : Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
    (V : (Over W)ᵒᵖ) :
    globalSectionVal (overGlobalSectionRestrict h g) V =
      globalSectionVal g (op ((Over.map h).obj V.unop)) := by
  unfold globalSectionVal overGlobalSectionRestrict
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

variable (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **A presentation of `ℐ|_U` by finitely many sections restricts to every object over `U`.**
If `ℐ|_U` is the sheaf of ideals generated by `f_1, …, f_r` on `𝒞/U`, then for every arrow
`h : W ⟶ U` the sheaf of ideals `ℐ|_W` on `𝒞/W` is the one generated by the restrictions of the
`f_i` along `h`.

Both inclusions are local statements read through `CategoryTheory.Over.map h : 𝒞/W ⥤ 𝒞/U`,
which acts as the identity on underlying objects of `𝒞` and therefore leaves all the rings of
sections, all the values of the generators, and all the restriction maps unchanged. The only
non-definitional step is that a sieve of `V` in `𝒞/W` covers as soon as its image under
`Over.map h` does, which is `CategoryTheory.Sieve.overEquiv_functorPullback_map`: both slice
topologies test a sieve by the sieve of `V.left` it induces on `𝒞`, and those two sieves of
`V.left` coincide. -/
theorem overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict {U W : X.C} (h : W ⟶ U)
    {r : ℕ} {f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})}
    (hf : overIdeal 𝓘 U = generatedIdealSheaf f) :
    overIdeal 𝓘 W = generatedIdealSheaf fun i ↦ overGlobalSectionRestrict h (f i) := by
  refine le_antisymm (SheafOfModules.Submodule.le_iff.2 fun V x hx ↦ ?_)
    (generatedIdealSheaf_le _ fun i V ↦ ?_)
  · obtain ⟨S, hS, hc⟩ := exists_sieve_of_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f (hf ▸ hx :
      x ∈ (generatedIdealSheaf f).obj (op ((Over.map h).obj V.unop)))
    refine mem_generatedIdealSheaf_of_locally _ (S := S.functorPullback (Over.map h)) ?_ ?_
    · show Sieve.overEquiv V.unop (S.functorPullback (Over.map h)) ∈ X.J V.unop.left
      rw [Sieve.overEquiv_functorPullback_map]
      exact hS
    · intro T g hg
      obtain ⟨c, hcw⟩ := hc ((Over.map h).map g) hg
      refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
      simp only [globalSectionVal_overGlobalSectionRestrict, unop_op]
      exact hcw
  · simp only [globalSectionVal_overGlobalSectionRestrict]
    have hmem := globalSectionVal_mem_generatedIdealSheaf f i (op ((Over.map h).obj V.unop))
    rw [← hf] at hmem
    exact hmem

/-- **The finitely-generated locus of a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`**: the objects `U` of the site
over which `ℐ|_U` is the sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many sections of `𝒪(U)`.

A global section of the structure sheaf of the slice site `𝒞/U` is the same thing as a section
of `𝒪` over `U`, the object `𝟙 : U ⟶ U` being terminal in `𝒞/U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection`); so this is the condition of
[Stacks, Tag 099E] that defines its subcategory `𝒞'`, in the spelling
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` that the Čech complex of
[Stacks, Tag 099B] is built from. -/
def IsFinitelyGeneratedOver (U : X.C) : Prop :=
  ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections ((X.over U).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w})),
    overIdeal 𝓘 U = generatedIdealSheaf f

/-- **The finitely-generated locus is stable under arrows**: finite generation of `ℐ` is a
local condition, so if `ℐ|_U` is generated by finitely many sections then so is `ℐ|_W` for
every `W` over `U`. This is `overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict`. -/
theorem IsFinitelyGeneratedOver.of_hom {U W : X.C} (hU : IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 U)
    (h : W ⟶ U) : IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 W :=
  let ⟨r, f, hf⟩ := hU
  ⟨r, _, overIdeal_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overGlobalSectionRestrict 𝓘 h hf⟩

/-- **A family of objects on which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections and which covers
the final object exhibits the finitely-generated locus as cover dense.** Every arrow into an
arbitrary object `U` whose source admits *some* arrow to a member of the family factors through
an object of the locus — namely its own source, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsFinitelyGeneratedOver.of_hom` — and the sieve of such arrows is
`CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofObjects`, which `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` says is
covering at every object. -/
theorem isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C}
    (hV : X.J.CoversTop V) (hfg : ∀ i, IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 (V i)) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).IsCoverDense X.J where
  is_cover U := by
    refine X.J.superset_covering (fun T p hp ↦ ?_) (hV U)
    obtain ⟨i, ⟨b⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff V p).1 hp
    exact ⟨⟨⟨T, (hfg i).of_hom 𝓘 b⟩, 𝟙 T, p, Category.id_comp p⟩⟩

/-- **Cover-density of the finitely-generated locus of a finite-type sheaf of ideals.** This is
the first step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E]: for `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` of finite type, *every* object
of `𝒞` is covered by objects on which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections, so the
inclusion of the full subcategory `𝒞'` of those objects is cover dense.

What the finite-type hypothesis supplies is only a family covering the *final* object,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`; but
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` is by definition a statement at every object,
and the locus is stable under arrows, so no relativisation of that construction to a slice is
needed. -/
theorem isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).IsCoverDense X.J := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, r, f, hf⟩ := exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 h
  exact isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘 hV fun i ↦ ⟨r i, f i, hf i⟩

/-- **The finitely-generated locus of a finite-type sheaf of ideals is a dense subsite.** With
the topology on `𝒞'` for which a sieve covers exactly when its image in `𝒞` does
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.restrictedTopology`, equal to
`CategoryTheory.Functor.inducedTopology` here), the inclusion `𝒞' ⟶ 𝒞` is a dense subsite: it
is cover dense by `isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType`, and it is locally
full and locally faithful because it is full and faithful.

This is the hypothesis of `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsDenseSubsite.sheafEquiv` and of
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestrictionEquivalence`, so sheaves of modules on `𝒞` and on
`𝒞'` have equivalent categories — the sense in which [Stacks, Tag 099E] may "replace `𝒞` by the
full subcategory on which `ℐ` is finitely generated". -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).IsDenseSubsite
      ((ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).restrictedTopology X.J) X.J :=
  let := isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 h
  inferInstance

/-- `isDenseSubsite_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType` for
`CategoryTheory.Functor.inducedTopology`, the finest topology on `𝒞'` making the inclusion
continuous; it coincides with the restricted topology here because the inclusion is cover
dense, and it is the topology at which Mathlib's Comparison Lemma
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafInducedTopologyEquivOfIsCoverDense` is stated. -/
theorem isDenseSubsite_inducedTopology_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType) :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).IsDenseSubsite
      ((ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).inducedTopology X.J) X.J :=
  let := isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 h
  inferInstance

section Instances

variable [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]

/-- `isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType` as an instance, so that the
dense-subsite transports apply to the inclusion of the finitely-generated locus without the
hypothesis being produced by hand. -/
instance isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_instance :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (IsFinitelyGeneratedOver 𝓘)).IsCoverDense X.J :=
  isCoverDense_ι_isFinitelyGeneratedOver_of_isFiniteType 𝓘 inferInstance

end Instances

end CoverDense

